> ### **The Future of Global Plastics Policy**
> The deadlock in multinational efforts to address plastic pollution highlights persistent challenges and the need for innovative solutions. Revamping negotiation strategies could unlock a pathway to a comprehensive treaty, with implications for both environmental sustainability and human health. Coordinating global policies will play a crucial role in mitigating one of the planet's most pervasive environmental problems. How stakeholders, including nations with varying levels of plastic production and waste management capabilities, come together will shape the success of these global efforts.
